WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.980
Rome, at night.

2
00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.310
Lightning splits the sky.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.220
A lion walks calmly near the Capitol.

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.490
Weeks earlier, a Soothsayer
called out a warning:

5
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.860
"Beware the Ides of March."

6
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.630
His wife dreams his
statue runs with blood,

7
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.510
and warns him: "When beggars die, there are
no comets seen;" Every sign says danger.

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.100
So was his death always going to happen?

9
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.140
In this mission, you'll
track every omen in the play,

10
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.620
from the Soothsayer to the final act.

11
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.730
You'll hear Caesar and Calphurnia
argue about fear and death.

12
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.990
And you'll ask what the characters
make of all these signs.

13
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: decide whether
Caesar's death was fated.
